# Two branches that each add an entry under "Unreleased" touch the same lines,
# so a plain merge stops at the rebase. Union keeps the lines of both sides,
# and a heading both sides add is kept once.
# The cost: union never reports a conflict. When both sides change the same
# line it keeps both and says nothing. A branch that started before a release
# can land its entry under the new version instead of under "Unreleased".
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
